  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4012c288",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a group of Black youth holding signs that say 'This is America. Count every vote,' which is a positive message about voting rights and civic participation. However, the overlaid text 'what if i told you blacks should not vote' is a hateful and racist statement that directly attacks Black people by suggesting they should be denied the fundamental democratic right to vote. This is a clear example of hate speech targeting a specific racial group, invoking historical and systemic racism against Black Americans. The juxtaposition of the positive civil rights imagery with the hateful text creates a deliberately provocative and offensive message intended to incite racism and undermine the legitimacy of Black political participation. The meme's intent is to spread hateful rhetoric by using the visual of a peaceful civil rights moment to contrast with a racist, exclusionary message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_830ee10a"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
